{
  "_id": "tg-rest",
  "content": [
    {
      "text": "he rested on the seventh day, Gen. 2:2 (Ex. 20:11; 31:17; Heb. 4:4; Moses 3:2; Abr. 5:2). seventh day thou shalt rest, Ex. 23:12 (34:21). seventh is the sabbath of rest, Ex. 31:15. presence shall go with thee, and I will give thee rest, Ex. 33:14. it is a year of rest unto the land, Lev. 25:5. Lord have given rest unto your brethren, Deut. 3:20. giveth you rest from all your enemies, Deut. 12:10. God hath given you rest, Josh. 1:13. land rested from war, Josh. 11:23 (14:15; Judg. 3:11, 30; 5:31). spirit of Elijah doth rest on Elisha, 2 Kgs. 2:15. in mine heart to build an house of rest, 1 Chr. 28:2. my flesh also shall rest in hope, Ps. 16:9 (Acts 2:26). Rest in the Lord, and wait patiently for him, Ps. 37:7. sware in my wrath that they should not enter into my rest, Ps. 95:11 (Heb. 3:11, 18). Correct thy son, and he shall give thee rest, Prov. 29:17. spirit of the Lord shall rest upon him, Isa. 11:2 (2 Ne. 21:2). root of Jesse … his rest shall be glorious, Isa. 11:10 (2 Ne. 21:10). rest wherewith ye may cause the weary to rest, Isa. 28:12. Spirit of the Lord caused him to rest, Isa. 63:14. where is the place of my rest, Isa. 66:1 (Acts 7:49). ye shall find rest for your souls, Jer. 6:16 (Matt. 11:29; Alma 37:34). thou shalt rest, Dan. 12:13.",
